1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,100
What if the best material changes when the
operating temperature changes?

2
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:10,100
Oxygen-ion conductors matter to electrochemical
technologies, but selection is conditional.

3
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:15,100
A choice at one temperature may change across a
device's working range.

4
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:20,100
Researchers also need comparable measurements,
explicit models and traceable evidence.

5
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:24,800
OxyProof brings those checks into a research
workbench that makes its limits visible.

6
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:30,800
We start with three published bulk-conductivity
records from the same curated source group.

7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,400
They share a reported method and measured range:
600 to 1100 kelvin.

8
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:39,800
At 700 kelvin, row one leads: one, then two, then
three.

9
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:48,700
Move the actual temperature control, and the
conditional model ordering begins to change.

10
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:54,300
At 1000 kelvin, row three leads: three, then two,
then one.

11
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:59,800
The result follows activation energies,
prefactors and the selected temperature regimes.

12
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,100
Analytical crossings are audited separately from
changes in the selected fitted regime.

13
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:10,700
The model intersections are near 776, 818 and 854
kelvin, inside valid joint regimes.

14
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:16,300
These are calculated intersections of fitted
models, not experimentally measured crossovers.

15
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:20,700
At a published T-star boundary, the affected
source row is withheld.

16
00:01:20,900 --> 00:01:24,800
No uncertainty bounds are available. Experimental
confirmation is needed.

17
00:01:25,300 --> 00:01:30,500
Next, we load saved traces from three genuine
DeepSeek API acceptance calls.

18
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:35,700
These executions were captured earlier; playback
makes no new model request.

19
00:01:35,900 --> 00:01:41,000
Scenario B asks how the named Huang group's
ranking changes with temperature.

20
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:46,300
DeepSeek Flash selected the allowlisted
temperature-interval analysis tool.

21
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:51,500
The interface shows the real provider identity
and the model-selected operation.

22
00:01:51,700 --> 00:01:57,000
Validated arguments retain 700 to 1000 kelvin,
bulk conductivity and three source rows.

23
00:01:57,200 --> 00:02:03,000
The model selects the tool. The validated physics
engine supplies the numerical results.

24
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:09,600
Independent auditing controls the verdict and
explains the validated result.

25
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:15,400
Now add demanding requirements: 600 degrees
Celsius and ten percent humidity.

26
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:20,700
Also require stability for ten thousand operating
hours, rather than just conductivity.

27
00:02:20,900 --> 00:02:26,000
The recorded model proposed screening and flagged
unsupported requirements.

28
00:02:26,200 --> 00:02:31,300
Independent validation checked the original
request, retaining humidity and lifetime.

29
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:36,600
The available records do not establish those
properties, so scientific execution was blocked.

30
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:42,000
No scientific calculation tool ran, and no
unsupported recommendation was produced.

31
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:46,100
The result is insufficient evidence, with a
proposed future measurement.

32
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:49,800
When evidence is missing, OxyProof refuses to
guess.

33
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:56,000
Every result remains tied to the published
dataset, original source rows and explicit units.

34
00:02:56,200 --> 00:03:01,800
The parameters, selected regimes and evidence
limits remain visible for researcher review.

35
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:08,800
Shared source metadata supports comparison, but
sample conditions still need review.

36
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:14,600
The actual JSON export preserves the source
records and deterministic calculation trace.

37
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:19,700
Warnings and code fingerprints travel with the
report, supporting offline reproduction.

38
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:25,200
OxyProof explains when the answer changes and why
it changes.

39
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:29,800
It also shows where the evidence stops, so a
researcher can decide what to check next.

40
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:34,600
AI can assist scientific decision-making without
being allowed to invent the science.
